{"The fetch_error_details function uses zip(error_ids, events.values()) to pair error IDs with their event data incorrectly - nodestore.backend.get_multi(node_ids) returns a dict keyed by node_id (not error_id), and dict values are not guaranteed to be in the same order as the input list. Additionally, if some events are missing from the nodestore, the returned dict will have fewer entries, causing the zip to misalign error IDs with the wrong event data, resulting in error titles, messages, and timestamps being attributed to the wrong error IDs.": 0.9654563665390015, "TableWidgetVisualization receives hardcoded empty data (columns={[]}, tableData={{data: [], meta: {fields: {}, units: {}}}}) when the use-table-widget-visualization feature flag is enabled, while StyledSimpleTableChart in the else branch correctly receives result.data and result.meta - enabling the feature flag would render empty tables instead of actual widget data.": 0.9965588450431824}